Revision history for Ekorn-Pipeline

Unreleased

    A pipeline can go where a stage goes, standing for its stages, so
    pipelines are built from pipelines without ->stages.

    It ships one roadmap item, 2026-0004. Nothing a pipeline did
    before changes: every message a pipeline gives today reads as it
    did, and DBIx::Squirrel can take it as it stands.

    - Ekorn::Pipeline->new takes a pipeline as a stage, composing its
      stages in place, as if its stages had been given there, so a take
      inside it takes from the whole run. Its stages are what its stages
      method returns, so a subclass that overrides it is composed as it
      says. (roadmap 2026-0004)
    - A stage inside a pipeline given as a stage is named in messages by
      its place in each pipeline, as "Pipeline stage #2.3 failed", and
      three deep "#1.2.3"; DIAGNOSTICS now shows "#%s" for these. A
      stage given directly is named as before. (roadmap 2026-0004)
    - is_stage, exported by Ekorn::Pipeline on request, is true for what
      new takes as a stage: a code reference or a pipeline. A function
      taking its stages off the end of its arguments can use it to take
      a pipeline there too. (roadmap 2026-0004)
    - The MetaCPAN and Kwalitee badges are in the README.

v0.1.2 2026-11-08

    The reference and the how-to on MetaCPAN, as POD manuals.

    It adds documentation only: the code is as in v0.1.1, and it ships
    no roadmap items.

    - The reference and the how-to ship as POD,
      Ekorn::Pipeline::Manual::Reference and
      Ekorn::Pipeline::Manual::HowTo, made from their Markdown, so
      MetaCPAN and perldoc have them with the modules.

v0.1.1 2026-11-08

    The pipeline from DBIx-Squirrel v2.0.2, on its own, so that any
    function can take stages from its caller.

    It ships three roadmap items, settled after v0.1.0's trial: a
    pipeline's stages can be spliced into another, with the stages
    method (2026-0001); an iterator ends once a stage dies (2026-0002);
    and a pipeline's count in scalar context is promised (2026-0003).

    - Requires Perl 5.36 or later.
    - Ekorn::Pipeline runs values through a list of stages, each a code
      reference given one value, in $_ and as its argument, and
      returning nothing (a filter), one value (a map) or several (a
      flatMap). A pipeline is called with values, or pulls them from a
      source with an iterator, calling it only as results are wanted.
    - Once a stage dies, an iterator has ended, as a pushed run has:
      every call after returns an empty list, and neither the source
      nor any end function is called again. In v0.1.0's trial it
      carried on, without the value that died. (roadmap 2026-0002)
    - Called in scalar context, a pipeline returns how many results
      came out, as an array would; the POD now promises it.
      (roadmap 2026-0003)
    - A pipeline's stages method returns its stages, so they can be
      spliced into another pipeline, or given to any function that
      takes stages, running as if listed there. (roadmap 2026-0001)
    - SECURITY.md says how to report a vulnerability, privately, and
      CONTRIBUTING.md how to report a bug or ask for a feature; the
      distribution takes issues, not pull requests.
    - Ekorn::Pipeline::Stop ends a pipeline early, passing on any
      values it carries, after which the source isn't called again. A
      stop not made by throw, and so not an array, carries nothing.
    - Ekorn::Pipeline::Gather makes a stage afresh for each run, with
      an optional end function, called once the values run out.
    - Ekorn::Pipeline::Pipes gives a class pipe and tap methods, which
      run the object through stages.
    - Canned stages: take, drop, take_while and drop_while in
      Ekorn::Pipeline::Stages::Flow; batch and collect in
      Ekorn::Pipeline::Stages::Batch; peek, count_into and dump_to in
      Ekorn::Pipeline::Stages::Taps.
    - A stage that dies is named by its place, at the caller's line, and
      so are mistakes in making a pipeline or a canned stage.
    - Modules of stages can live under any namespace: general stages
      under Ekorn::Pipeline::Stages, and those for one kind of value or
      source with the module that knows about it, built from Gather,
      Stop and croakf, which reports at the caller's line.
    - Versions: a v0.1.x only fixes or adds. A change to how stages
      behave, or a public name dropped or renamed, waits for v0.2.0.
    - A how-to, docs/HOWTO.md, with recipes for callers, function
      authors and stage authors, and a reference, docs/REFERENCE.md,
      describing every module and how a pipeline behaves, with notes
      for stage authors. Both are on GitHub, linked from the README.
